  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Given below are two statements : one is labelled as Assertion&nbsp;and the other is labelled as Reason.</p><p><strong>Assertion:</strong> The ionic radii of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Mg</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> are same.</p><p><strong>Reason:</strong> Both <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Mg</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> are isoelectronic species.</p><p>In the light of the above statements, choose the correct answer from the options given below.</p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "19QXB",
      "text": "Both&nbsp;Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion.",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "WtzJH",
      "text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion.",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "gXjyR",
      "text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "CuTrG",
      "text": "Assertion is false but Reason is true.",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Both&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Mg</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;have&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn></math>&nbsp;electrons each and they are isoelectronic species.</p><p>But the size of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;is greater than&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Mg</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;as&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>size</mi><mo>&#8733;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>of</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>Mg</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>12</mn><mn>10</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>of</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>8</mn><mn>10</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>Number</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>of</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>protons</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>Number</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>of</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>electrons</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p>",
